{
  "about": "Engine contract: every editor internal that web/xr-host.js, the app (EditorWebView.swift) and the CI hooks rely on. An editor update that renames or drops one must fail CI loudly instead of silently breaking the touch UI. Checked twice: scripts/check_contract.py (build step: each entry's token must still appear in the packaged editors' code) and the Autotest 'contract' hook (EditorUITests: in each of the four running editors, every entry that applies to that editor and device must exist). Kinds: global = dotted path from the editor frame's window (optional 'equals'); api = method of the editor API (window.__xrApi); dom = CSS selector present once the document is open; controller = app controller (DE / SSE / PE / PDFE .getController(name)) with an optional dotted 'path' inside it; callback / setting / id = static only (engine callback names, InternalSettings or localStorage keys, DOM ids made later, e.g. when a menu first opens). 'editors' (word / cell / slide / pdf) and 'devices' (phone / tablet) limit the runtime check; 'static': false skips the token check (a name that only exists at runtime). Add an entry here with every new engine symbol xr-host.js uses.",
